Vulkan and WebGPU: instance data finds its location past i_data9

A vertex shader's attribute list (written by shaderc after the code) lists the shader's inputs in the order of
their locations, and the Vulkan and WebGPU renderers take an attribute's place in it as its location. Instance data
had a bare UINT16_MAX there, and the renderers placed instance vec4 N at the first location after the attributes
plus N. glslang maps input locations in name order, though: i_data10 and i_data11 come before i_data2, so a shader
with more than ten instance vec4s read the wrong data from i_data2 on (Metal finds them by name and was right).

shaderc now writes which i_data each instance entry is (ids from 0x0100, instanceDataToId), and the two renderers
take each instance vec4's location from its place in the list. A shader compiled before keeps its UINT16_MAX
entries, which are taken in order as before; renderers that know no instance ids count them as instance data as
they did.

